From: DroidDeck
Date: 2026-11-20
Subject: steamcompmgr: paint before presenting a held rotation buffer

A client commit that selects a rotation buffer must be painted before it is
presented. When a held base commit arrives without any repaint flag, the normal
path presents the slot without painting it and stale content reaches the
display. This is the same "catch-up frame without repaint" bug fixed for KWin by
Droidspaces-Mali's anland patch 0002 (119 commits without a render out of ~3000
frames before, 2396 frames from 2396 renders after). Marking these commits as
needing a paint makes present follow render rather than substituting an
unpainted buffer.

--- a/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
+++ b/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
@@ -10566,6 +10566,14 @@ steamcompmgr_main(int argc, char **argv)
 			else
 				eFlipType = FlipType::Normal;
 
+			// DroidDeck: a client commit that selects a rotation buffer must be painted before it
+			// is presented. When a held base commit arrives without any repaint flag, the normal
+			// path below presents the slot without painting it and stale content reaches the
+			// display (the same "catch-up frame without repaint" bug fixed in Droidspaces-Mali's
+			// anland patch 0002). Marking these commits as needing a paint makes present follow
+			// render rather than substituting an unpainted buffer.
+			const bool bHasHeldBaseCommit = pPaintFocus && pPaintFocus->HeldCommits[HELD_COMMIT_BASE] != nullptr;
+
 			bool bShouldPaint = false;
 
 			//if ( GetBackend()->IsVisible() )
@@ -10575,7 +10583,7 @@ steamcompmgr_main(int argc, char **argv)
 				{
 					case FlipType::Normal:
 					{
-						bShouldPaint = vblank && ( hasRepaint || hasRepaintNonBasePlane || bForceSyncFlip );
+						bShouldPaint = vblank && ( hasRepaint || hasRepaintNonBasePlane || bForceSyncFlip || bHasHeldBaseCommit );
 						break;
 					}
 
